{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "nebula-api-collection",
		"name": "Nebula API",
		"description": "Complete API collection for the Nebula Backend.\n\n## Setup\n1. Set the `baseUrl` variable (default: `http://localhost:4000`)\n2. Start with **Register** then **Login**\n3. The login request auto-saves `accessToken` and `refreshToken` to collection variables\n4. Authenticated requests use `{{accessToken}}` automatically via Bearer token\n\n## Auth Flow\n1. Register → Check email for verification token\n2. Verify Email (paste the token)\n3. Login → tokens are saved automatically\n4. Use authenticated endpoints (me, logout, change-password)\n\n## OAuth Flow\n- Open `{{baseUrl}}/auth/github` in a browser to initiate GitHub OAuth",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "baseUrl",
			"value": "http://localhost:4000",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "accessToken",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "refreshToken",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "testEmail",
			"value": "test@example.com",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "testPassword",
			"value": "Test1234!@",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "verificationToken",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "resetToken",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "repositoryId",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "Auth - Public",
			"description": "Public authentication endpoints (no token required)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n    \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\",\n    \"fullName\": \"Test User\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "register"]
						},
						"description": "Register a new user account.\n\n**Body:**\n- `email` (required): Valid email address\n- `password` (required): Min 8 characters\n- `fullName` (optional): User's display name\n\nA verification email will be sent to the provided email."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Registration successful', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Returns userId', function () {",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.data.userId).to.be.a('string');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Login",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\",\n    \"password\": \"{{testPassword}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
						},
						"description": "Login with email and password.\n\n**Body:**\n- `email` (required): Registered email\n- `password` (required): Account password\n\nReturns access & refresh tokens. Tokens are also set as HTTP-only cookies."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Login successful', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Auto-save tokens to collection variables",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"if (json.data && json.data.data) {",
									"    const data = json.data.data;",
									"    if (data.accessToken) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', data.accessToken);",
									"        console.log('✅ accessToken saved');",
									"    }",
									"    if (data.refreshToken) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);",
									"        console.log('✅ refreshToken saved');",
									"    }",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Verify Email",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"token\": \"{{verificationToken}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/verify-email",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "verify-email"]
						},
						"description": "Verify email address using the token sent to the user's email.\n\n**Body:**\n- `token` (required): Verification token from email\n\n💡 **Tip:** Copy the token from the verification email and paste it into the `verificationToken` collection variable, or directly into the body."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Email verified', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Forgot Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"email\": \"{{testEmail}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "forgot-password"]
						},
						"description": "Request a password reset email.\n\n**Body:**\n- `email` (required): Registered email address\n\nAlways returns success to prevent email enumeration attacks."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Forgot password request sent', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Reset Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"token\": \"{{resetToken}}\",\n    \"newPassword\": \"NewPassword123!\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "reset-password"]
						},
						"description": "Reset password using the token from the reset email.\n\n**Body:**\n- `token` (required): Reset token from email\n- `newPassword` (required): New password (min 8 characters)\n\n💡 **Tip:** Copy the token from the reset email and paste it into the `resetToken` collection variable."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Password reset successful', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Refresh Tokens",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{refreshToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "refresh"]
						},
						"description": "Refresh the access and refresh tokens using the current refresh token.\n\nSends the refresh token via `Authorization: Bearer` header.\n\nReturns new token pair and updates cookies."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Tokens refreshed', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Auto-save new tokens",
									"const json = pm.response.json();",
									"if (json.data && json.data.data) {",
									"    const data = json.data.data;",
									"    if (data.accessToken) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', data.accessToken);",
									"        console.log('✅ accessToken refreshed');",
									"    }",
									"    if (data.refreshToken) {",
									"        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);",
									"        console.log('✅ refreshToken refreshed');",
									"    }",
									"}"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Auth - Protected",
			"description": "Authenticated endpoints (requires access token)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get My Profile",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "me"]
						},
						"description": "Get the authenticated user's profile.\n\nReturns user info with linked OAuth accounts (sensitive fields stripped)."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Profile retrieved', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.data).to.have.property('email');",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.data).to.have.property('id');",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test('Sensitive fields excluded', function () {",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.data).to.not.have.property('password');",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.data).to.not.have.property('refreshToken');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Change Password",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							},
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"currentPassword\": \"{{testPassword}}\",\n    \"newPassword\": \"NewSecurePass123!\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "change-password"]
						},
						"description": "Change password for the authenticated user.\n\n**Body:**\n- `currentPassword` (required): Current account password\n- `newPassword` (required): New password (min 8 characters)\n\n⚠️ Only works for accounts with a password (not OAuth-only accounts)."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Password changed', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"name": "Logout",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "auth", "logout"]
						},
						"description": "Logout the authenticated user.\n\nClears the stored refresh token and auth cookies."
					},
					"response": [],
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('Logged out', function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"    const json = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(json.data.success).to.be.true;",
									"});",
									"",
									"// Clear saved tokens",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', '');",
									"pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', '');",
									"console.log('🗑️ Tokens cleared');"
								]
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Auth - OAuth",
			"description": "OAuth authentication flows (browser-based)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GitHub OAuth (Open in Browser)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/github",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["auth", "github"]
						},
						"description": "⚠️ **Open this URL in a browser**, not Postman!\n\nInitiates the GitHub OAuth flow. You'll be redirected to GitHub to authorize, then redirected back with tokens.\n\nThe callback URL is: `{{baseUrl}}/auth/github/callback`\n\nAfter successful auth, you'll be redirected to the frontend with tokens in the URL query params."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "GitHub OAuth Callback",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/github/callback?code=GITHUB_AUTH_CODE",
							"host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
							"path": ["auth", "github", "callback"],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "code",
									"value": "GITHUB_AUTH_CODE",
									"description": "GitHub OAuth authorization code (auto-provided by GitHub redirect)"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "GitHub OAuth callback endpoint.\n\n⚠️ This is called automatically by GitHub after authorization. You don't need to call it manually.\n\nThe `code` parameter is provided by GitHub's OAuth redirect."
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "Repositories",
			"description": "Endpoints to fetch, import, list, analyze, and delete user repositories.\n\n## Analysis flow\n1. Import a repository (or list imported ones)\n2. Set `repositoryId` collection variable to the imported repo UUID\n3. **Analyze Repository** — starts an async BullMQ job (returns immediately)\n4. **Get Analysis Status** — poll until status is `COMPLETED` or `FAILED`",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get GitHub Repositories",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/github?force=false&page=1&limit=30",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"github"
							],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "force",
									"value": "false",
									"description": "Bypass in-memory cache if true"
								},
								{
									"key": "page",
									"value": "1",
									"description": "Page number (optional)"
								},
								{
									"key": "limit",
									"value": "30",
									"description": "Items per page (optional)"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "List the user's public and private repositories live from the GitHub REST API.\n\nRequires access token and a connected GitHub OAuth account."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Import Repository",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							},
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"githubRepoId\": \"123456789\",\n    \"name\": \"my-cool-project\",\n    \"owner\": \"octocat\",\n    \"defaultBranch\": \"main\",\n    \"isPrivate\": false,\n    \"cloneUrl\": \"https://github.com/octocat/my-cool-project.git\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/import",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"import"
							]
						},
						"description": "Imports a selected repository metadata row into the database with status `IMPORTED`."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Imported Repositories",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories"
							]
						},
						"description": "List all repositories imported into the database by the authenticated user."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Repository Details",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/{{repositoryId}}",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"{{repositoryId}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Retrieve metadata details for one imported repository.\n\nSet the `repositoryId` collection variable to the imported repo UUID."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Analyze Repository",
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/{{repositoryId}}/analyze",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"{{repositoryId}}",
								"analyze"
							]
						},
						"description": "Start an async analysis job for an imported repository.\n\nThe controller only enqueues the job and returns immediately. Pipeline stages:\n1. Clone repository\n2. Repository discovery\n3. Graphify analysis\n4. Normalize output\n5. Build knowledge graph\n6. Save to Neo4j\n7. Cleanup workspace\n\nReturns an `AnalysisJob` with status `QUEUED`. Poll **Get Analysis Status** for progress.\n\nRequires Redis (BullMQ) and a linked GitHub OAuth account for cloning."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Analysis Status",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/{{repositoryId}}/analysis",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"{{repositoryId}}",
								"analysis"
							]
						},
						"description": "Get the latest analysis job for a repository (for polling).\n\n**Job status:** `QUEUED` | `RUNNING` | `COMPLETED` | `FAILED`\n\n**Stage examples:** `queued`, `workspace`, `clone`, `discovery`, `graphify`, `normalize`, `build_graph`, `save_neo4j`, `done`\n\nOn failure, `error` contains the message."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "Delete Imported Repository",
					"request": {
						"method": "DELETE",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/repositories/{{repositoryId}}",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api",
								"repositories",
								"{{repositoryId}}"
							]
						},
						"description": "Remove the imported repository metadata row from the database."
					},
					"response": []
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
